May Agni the gārhapatya fire protect her;
may he make her offspring attain old age.
With an unoccupied lap, may she be the mother of living children;
may she awaken to joy in grandsons. Svāhā!

May no cry arise in your house at night;
may weeping women lodge elsewhere than with you.
Do not beat your breast, weeping;
as a woman whose husband lives, shine in your husband's world,
looking upon your offspring well disposed. Svāhā!

Step onto this stone;
be firm like a stone.
Thrust away the enemy;
and do not be beneath enemies.

This woman speaks
as she casts fried grains into the fire:
"May my husband be long-lived;
may he live a hundred years;
may my kinsmen prosper." Svāhā!

Become a friend who has taken seven steps;
may I attain your friendship;
may I not be separated from your friendship;
may you not be separated from my friendship.

May Prajāpati produce offspring for us;
may Aryaman unite [us] until old age.
Free from ill fortune, enter your husband's world;
bring peace to our bipeds, peace to our quadrupeds.

May [he] place your heart in my vow;
may your mind follow my mind;
single-minded, delight in my word;
may Bṛhaspati join you to me.

Mount the bright-flowered, cotton-wood [chariot], multiform,
golden-hued, well-wrought, with fine wheels, O Sūryā;
[mount] the navel of immortality; make an easy bridal journey for your husband.

May the highwaymen not find
the couple who approach together;
by easy paths may they cross the difficult [way];
may the hostile ones run away.

Here is steadfastness, here is self-steadfastness;
here is delight, take delight here;
in me is steadfastness, in me is self-steadfastness;
in me is delight, take delight in me.

May Viṣṇu prepare the womb;
may Tvaṣṭṛ shape the forms;
may Prajāpati pour in;
may Dhātṛ place the embryo in you.

Place the embryo, Sinīvālī;
place the embryo, Sarasvatī;
may both divine Aśvins, garlanded with blue lotuses,
place the embryo in you.

Male are Mitra and Varuṇa;
male are both Aśvins;
male are Agni and Vāyu;
male is the embryo in your belly.

Male is Agni, male is Indra,
male is the divine Bṛhaspati;
obtain a male son;
let a male be born after him.

With which Prajāpati parts the parting of Aditi
for great good fortune,
with that I part her parting;
I make her offspring reach old age.

I invoke Rākā, easy to call, with fair praise;
may the fortunate one hear us and take heed herself;
may she sew the work with an unbroken needle;
may she grant a heroic chief lasting a hundred lives.

The wise one took away the tail;
Dhātṛ brought it back again.
Go away, O wise one;
a male this one will be born,
named [such a one].

May Mitra and Varuṇa grant you intelligence;
may Agni grant you intelligence;
may both divine Aśvins, garlanded with blue lotuses,
grant you intelligence.

May that [month] hand you over to the day;
may the day hand you over to the night;
may the night hand you over to day and night;
may day and night hand you over to the half-months;
may the half-months hand you over to the months;
may the months hand you over to the seasons;
may the seasons hand you over to the year;
may the year hand you over to life and old age, [such a one].

O Agni, lord of vows, I shall perform a vow;
that I proclaim to you;
may I be able to do that; may I succeed through that.
Here I go from falsehood to truth. Svāhā!

O Vāyu, lord of vows, I shall perform a vow;
that I proclaim to you;
may I be able to do that; may I succeed through that.
Here I go from falsehood to truth. Svāhā!

O Sūrya, lord of vows, I shall perform a vow;
that I proclaim to you;
may I be able to do that; may I succeed through that.
Here I go from falsehood to truth. Svāhā!

O Moon, lord of vows, I shall perform a vow;
that I proclaim to you;
may I be able to do that; may I succeed through that.
Here I go from falsehood to truth. Svāhā!

We have joined together with the newcomer;
ward off the well-disposed mortal [from harm].
May we move about unhurt;
may this [youth] walk in well-being.

Agni has seized your hand;
Savitṛ has seized your hand;
Aryaman has seized your hand.
You are Mitra through [your] duty;
Agni is your teacher.

May my faculty come back to me;
may life come back, may fortune come back;
may wealth come back to me;
may brahminhood come back to me.

For glory, for fiery energy, for sacred radiance,
for strength, for faculty, for vigor, for proper food,
for increase of wealth, for brilliance, for reverence.

You are the world, thousandfold;
Sṛma gave you to Indra,
unbroken, uninjured, giving refreshment.

You are the nourisher of cattle, you rule over the increase of cattle; for the increase of cattle [I touch] you.
You are the nourisher of a thousand, you rule over the increase of a thousand;
for the increase of a thousand [I touch] you.

Soma is king; the Soma-clump is king;
Soma is our king; we belong to Soma.
You are the crusher of serpents, belonging to the Soma-clump;
belonging to the Soma-clump, you are the crusher of serpents.

Do not injure us in our children, in our offspring, or in our life;
do not injure us in our cows, nor in our horses.
Do not slay our warriors in anger, O Rudra;
bearing oblations, we call upon you continually.

I offer the full offering for glory;
whoever sacrifices to him, [the god] gives him a boon.
I choose a boon; I shine with glory in the world. Svāhā!

[…] Indra […];
darkness is before you;
I am light for you;
come unto me, all of you! Svāhā!

Swift one, protect me! Protector, protect me
from curses, from enemies;
you are the path of well-being!

The smallest of worms has been slain;
slain is the mother, slain the father;
and broken is their vessel
which was their storehouse of poison!

Release the cow from the fetter, O Varuṇa;
bind him who hates me;
slay him and that one, both of them!
Release the cow: let it eat grass, let it drink water!
